<% 
  const year = typeof currentYear !== 'undefined' ? currentYear : (typeof seo !== 'undefined' && seo.year ? seo.year : new Date().getFullYear());
%>
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>Nigerian University Grading System & Academic Guide (<%= year %>)</title>

    <!-- ✅ Advanced SEO Meta Tags -->
    <meta name="description" content="Understand the Nigerian university 5.0 GPA scale, grading system, class of degree classifications, carryover policies, and hostel application procedures in <%= year %>.">
    <meta name="keywords" content="Nigerian university grading system, GPA scale Nigeria <%= year %>, carryover meaning, class of degree, NUC grading scale">
    <meta name="author" content="MySchoolGist">
    <link rel="canonical" href="https://mysearch-query.onrender.com/schools/grading/system">

    <%- include('../includeFolder/_headers.ejs') %>
</head>
<body>
    
    <div class="container">
    <section class="section-txt">
        <h1>Nigerian University Grading System & Academic Guide (<%= year %>)</h1>
        <h2>Understanding "Carryover"</h2>
        <p>A "carryover" occurs when a student fails to score the minimum pass mark in a compulsory course during an academic semester and must retake it in a subsequent session.</p>
    </section>
    
    <section class="section-txt">
        <h2>Grading System & GPA Scale</h2>
        <p>Most Nigerian universities operate on a 5.0 Grade Point Average (GPA) grading scale structured as follows:</p>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>A (70 - 100%)</strong>: 5.0 Points (Excellent)</li>
            <li><strong>B (60 - 69%)</strong>: 4.0 Points (Very Good)</li>
            <li><strong>C (50 - 59%)</strong>: 3.0 Points (Good)</li>
            <li><strong>D (45 - 49%)</strong>: 2.0 Points (Fair)</li>
            <li><strong>E (40 - 44%)</strong>: 1.0 Point (Pass)</li>
            <li><strong>F (0 - 39%)</strong>: 0.0 Points (Fail)</li>
        </ul>
    </section>
    
    <section class="section-txt">
        <h2>Degree Classification Breakdown</h2>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>First Class:</strong> CGPA of 4.50 – 5.00</li>
            <li><strong>Second Class Upper (2:1):</strong> CGPA of 3.50 – 4.49</li>
            <li><strong>Second Class Lower (2:2):</strong> CGPA of 2.40 – 3.49</li>
            <li><strong>Third Class:</strong> CGPA of 1.50 – 2.39</li>
        </ul>
    </section>
</div>

